  281: 	#  disarmed for a probe with NO behaviour change at all: quote the pin
  282: 	#  literal (`"32"` instead of `32`) and regress/lib.sh:82 compares it as a
  283: 	#  string exactly as before, while this file silently stops governing that
  284: 	#  probe.  A two-word label or a hoisted variable does the same.
  285: 	#
  286: 	#  *** THIS WAS A RATCHET WITH A FLOOR OF 16 AND THE MEASURED VALUE WAS 18.
  287: 	#  A HAND-MAINTAINED RATCHET IS ITSELF AN UNRATCHETED NUMBER. ***
  288: 	#
  289: 	#  The old comment said "raise the floor when it rises, never lower it".  That
  290: 	#  instruction was silently missed TWICE -- the count went 16 -> 17 -> 18 while
  291: 	#  the floor stayed at 16 -- so two whole gate blocks carrying score-claim pins
  292: 	#  could have been deleted with this check still printing `good`.  Measured
  293: 	#  2026-08-26 by the seat answering `gateflr`.
