  636: 	printf '%s\n' "$rsout" | grep -E 'STALE|ROW_STATES_FAIL|^ ' | sed 's/^/          /'
  637: fi
  638: 
  639: #  ---- X ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  640: #  A CITED MEASUREMENT MUST EXIST.  The rule "a score claim names its artifact" was
  641: #  already in force and already being followed when it failed TWICE in one day:
  642: #
  643: #    * `#462` cited `probe_base.raw` for 52/52; a later 57-row table REUSED that name,
  644: #      so the claim became CONTRADICTED BY ITS OWN EVIDENCE, not merely unverifiable.
  645: #    * `#461`'s lethal mutant `m_dmarevert` (22/31) has NO per-row artifact at all --
  646: #      0 candidate lines across every `.out` in both scratchpads.  A retrospective audit
  647: #      of that detector was ATTEMPTED on 2026-08-24 and could not run.
  648: #
  649: #  EXISTENCE ONLY, and the scope cut is the safety argument.  It does not parse the log
  650: #  or re-derive the score: section U already checks DENOMINATORS against the gate pin,
  651: #  nothing mechanical can tell a measured numerator from a carried one, and a checker
  652: #  that tried would grow without bound -- the #392 shape.  A gate that stats cited paths
  653: #  cannot creep into policing scratch directories.
  654: #
  655: #  Specified by the fable5 adjudication of #462, Decision 4c, which set both the altitude
  656: #  ("checks committed records, never scratchpad state") and the scope cut.  Forward-only
  657: #  from round 462; earlier blocks predate the rule, and a red that no edit can clear is
  658: #  its own hazard.  NEGATIVE-CONTROLLED ON ITS FIRST RUN: it reported two missing
  659: #  artifacts, both real, and went green only after they were archived to a durable path.
  660: say ""; say "X. every measurement cited in a round block still exists"
  661: CACHK=$_HERE/pipeline/check_cited_artifacts.py
  662: if [ ! -f "$CACHK" ]; then
  663: 	bad "check_cited_artifacts.py MISSING -- cited measurements are NOT verified"
  664: elif caout=$(python "$CACHK" 2>&1); then
  665: 	good "$(printf '%s' "$caout" | grep -E 'CITED_ARTIFACTS_PASS')"
  666: else
  667: 	bad "A ROUND BLOCK CITES A MEASUREMENT THAT DOES NOT EXIST:"
  668: 	printf '%s\n' "$caout" | grep -E 'CITED_ARTIFACTS_FAIL|^    #' | sed 's/^/          /'
  669: 	bad "  restore the artifact, or correct the claim to say the log was not preserved"
  670: fi
  671: 
  672: #  THE SELFTEST FIRES ONLY WHEN THE CHECKER ITSELF CHANGES -- the section-R idiom, and
  673: #  wired the same way.  A completeness check found that this gate shipped WITHOUT one
  674: #  while both its siblings have them: the gate enforcing "every score names verifiable
  675: #  evidence" had no evidence of its own correctness, and the three false-green fixes it
  676: #  went through had nothing pinning them.  ***  IT FAILED ON ITS FIRST RUN AND FOUND A
  677: #  REAL BUG: *** `LOOSE` had been compiled with a literal BACKSPACE byte where `\\b`
  678: #  belonged, so the unenforced-mentions denominator matched NOTHING and had been printing
  679: #  a PHANTOM ZERO all evening -- in the counter added specifically to make phantom zeros
  680: #  visible.  UNTRACKED COUNTS AS TOUCHED, per section R's own scar.
  681: #  DETECT THE TOUCH INLINE, exactly as section R does -- `$CHANGED` is not defined
  682: #  until much later in this file, so the first version of this block never fired.
  683: #  UNTRACKED COUNTS AS TOUCHED: section R's own scar is that a checker was untracked
  684: #  on the very commit that introduced it, so neither diff could see it and the one
  685: #  commit that most needed the selftest was the one that skipped it.
  686: _catouched=$( { git diff --cached --name-only; git diff --name-only; git ls-files --others --exclude-standard; } | grep -c 'tools/pipeline/check_cited_artifacts\.py' )
  687: if [ "$_catouched" -gt 0 ]; then
  688: 	if stout=$(python "$CACHK" --selftest 2>&1); then
  689: 		good "$(printf '%s' "$stout" | grep -E 'SELFTEST_PASS')"
  690: 	else
  691: 		bad "check_cited_artifacts.py SELFTEST FAILED -- the gate is not trustworthy:"
  692: 		printf '%s\n' "$stout" | grep -E 'SELFTEST_FAIL|^    ' | sed 's/^/          /'
  693: 	fi
  694: else
  695: 	good "checker unchanged -- selftest not re-run (fires when it is edited)"
  696: fi
  697: 
  698: #  ---- J ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

