tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:2: """Regenerate the CODEX WALL section of fable_queue.md FROM THE LEDGER.
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:4: WHY: section I of `precommit_check.sh` requires that every `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: ...]` marker
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:5: is also NAMED IN THE QUEUE -- "holding a stage and queueing it are ONE action, not two."  That
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:6: is the right rule, and it fired three times in one evening because the list was maintained BY
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:7: HAND: each new panel added held markers, and the queue entry had to be edited to match.
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:9: A hand-maintained list of machine-readable facts is a list that goes stale, and this project
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:10: has the receipts: `RESUME.md` went stale for 26 rounds, the SEAT LEDGER for five days, the
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:11: `gate_offline.sh` floor comment said "16 -> 17" while the code read 18.  The queue entry was
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:12: about to join them.
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:14: So the section is DERIVED.  Run this after recording a panel; it rewrites exactly the block
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:15: between the two markers below and touches nothing else in the file.
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:17:     python tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py          rewrite the section
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:18:     python tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py --check  exit 1 if the file is out of date
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:20: WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO: it does not invent the prose.  The narrative paragraphs --
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:21: why the wall is one outage, what it blocks, the standing authority to proceed -- are written by
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:22: a human and live INSIDE the generated block as a constant here, because they are judgement.
tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:23: Only the ROW LIST and the COUNT are derived.  A generator that wrote the reasoning too would be
