class="ph st-held"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-held"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">pcheck</span><span class="ttl">pcheck  The pre-commit check cannot see any python detector, or a file named without its directory</span><sup class="b b-A">A</sup><span class="tip">pcheck  The pre-commit check cannot see any python detector, or a file named without its directory — HOLD: measured on its own run during round R1 — Found while committing R1, and it is the vacuity class this project tracks: the check reported two green lines about work it cannot see. Check E looks only for regress/diff_*.c (precommit_check.sh:155), so it has never seen ANY python detector - not selftest_logdir.py (added by R1), not selftest_absorb.py (shipped by r421), not readiness_predicate_test.py. Check C extracts paths with a pattern that needs both a src/, regress/ or man/ prefix AND a .c, .h, .sh or .1 extension (:92), so a message that names drive_guest.py, or names a file without its directory, cross-checks NOTHING and prints &#x27;message cites no source paths&#x27;. Both lines say ok where they should say not applicable. Self-review disclosed: the author of the round found it in the round&#x27;s own output. THIRD BLIND SPOT, measured on the follow-up commit: check D printed &#x27;no new file:line citations&#x27; while that commit added a dozen (drive_guest.py:207, :211, :222-224, :406-421, :435, lib.sh:31) - it does not scan .md files or the message itself, which is exactly where this project&#x27;s citations live.</span></span><span class="state st-held" title="measured on its own run during round R1">held</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-held"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><sup class="b b-A">A</sup><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — CONFIRMED — the author did this review (shown, not hidden) — REAL - measured on the R1 commit itself: check E printed &#x27;no detector added or modified&#x27; while the diff added one, and check C printed &#x27;cites no source paths&#x27; while the message cited five.</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-26 — *** VERDICT: KEEP OPEN. The python half is PARTLY closed by a different tool; the directory half is UNCHANGED and now WORSE; and it MEASURED A FOURTH BLIND SPOT THE ROW DOES NOT NAME, which makes check D vacuous on the normal commit path. *** LINE NUMBERS: the row cites :155 and :92, and at HEAD they are :970 and :907 -- ~800 lines of drift with the TEXT IDENTICAL. It reconciled this explicitly as intra-file growth rather than the wrong-tree signature (which shifts arms and changes which cases exist). PYTHON HALF, split answer: check E is unchanged and can never see a python file, but section R&#x27;s check_probe_wiring.py sees all 56 python artefacts. **They answer different questions** -- E asks whether a detector carries an identity guard, R asks whether anything runs it -- so the gap is real but narrower than recorded. For a python probe the identity-guard analogue is a gate-side `rows run` pin, **and nothing requires a new probe to have one**. *** THAT IS THE SAME HOLE AS `gateflr`, and one extension to check_probe_wiring.py closes both. *** DIRECTORY HALF, unchanged and BROADER than the row says: check C&#x27;s prefix alternation is `(src|regress|man)`, so **the entire `tools/` tree is invisible** -- precommit_check.sh cannot cross-check a commit message naming ITSELF, or panel.sh, or any pipeline checker. The alternation predates the 2026-08-17 harness migration into git, so this is NEW, not a restatement. It tabulated nine representative strings; `regress/drive_guest.py`, `tools/...`, and bare filenames are all invisible. The false-green is still there verbatim: no match -&gt; `good &quot;message cites no source paths&quot;`, an ok line about a message it could not read. *** THE FOURTH BLIND SPOT: CHECK D AUDITS A DIFFERENT CHANGE SET FROM EVERY OTHER SECTION. *** `$CHANGED` prefers `git diff --cached`; check D uses BARE `git diff -U0` -- unstaged only, always. Sections R and V both use BOTH and carry a comment saying they learned it the hard way. **So on the ordinary workflow -- git add, run precommit, commit -- `$ADDED` is EMPTY and both of D&#x27;s sub-checks print green about a diff they never read.** Its negative control for that is elegant and uses material already in the tree: the two stale `.sh:NNN` citations it found in check_probe_wiring.py&#x27;s docstring are exactly what a widened check must name, plus a correct `.sh:NNN` that must stay green so the check is not merely &#x27;reject all shell citations&#x27;. — evidence: Agent(model=opus) held-stage seat, batch A (harness rows). Read-only; GXEMUL-SEC only.</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-20 — MANUAL — WALL DISCHARGED -- re-fired 2026-08-20 after codex answered a health test (CODEX_ALIVE_20260820, and it got the arithmetic right). Verified a REAL review, not the echo that preceded it: delta over the brief is well past the ~688-byte banner and the usage-limit string is absent from the tail.
tools/pipeline\matrix.html:863:CLAIM 1 -- &#x27;not introduced by #430&#x27; -- MEASURED FALSE. Built from `git show 2458cfb^:src/cpus/memory_rw.c`, stock otherwise: the same guest program produces NO exception, NO restart, ONE device write. Pre-#430 the tail was silently mis-applied to the physically-following location -- the defect #430 fixed -- so there was nothing to restart. **#430 CREATED the fault, and the double-application is a direct consequence of it.**
tools/pipeline\matrix.html:881:The re-ranking DOWN is right, and there is a FOURTH reason the re-measurement did not state: the &#x27;fix may be wrong&#x27; caveat does not transfer to [[sh4bcr]], and that asymmetry is the ranking argument. mrwstore2 is blocked because real PowerPC hardware may genuinely do partial-completion-with-restart and there is no manual. No such ambiguity exists for a width-check exit(1): no SH-4 silicon powers off the machine because software used the wrong access width, so that fix needs no citation this project cannot obtain. — evidence: git show 0447c2e --stat; content search for 1201fffe</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-held"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-held"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">optrow</span><span class="ttl">optrow  Any row measuring a RESOURCE is only as good as the optimisation it pins</span><span class="tip">optrow  Any row measuring a RESOURCE is only as good as the optimisation it pins — commits: fd0ddef — HOLD: audit the other resource-measuring rows</span></span><span class="state st-held" title="audit the other resource-measuring rows">held</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-held"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — CONFIRMED — *** THE SIBLING OF constblind, AND IT COST A VACUOUS ROW. *** &#x27;The split is a loop, not recursion&#x27; was asserted by measuring stack growth -- and gcc 15.2.1 eliminates the tail call at -O2, so the recursion mutant measured 96 bytes and the row PASSED under the exact defect it existed to catch. One flag on that differential&#x27;s compile (-fno-optimize-sibling-calls) makes it real: loop 0 bytes, recursion 1,572,768. Where constblind was a row following the CONSTANT, this is a row following the COMPILER. Every row in regress/ that measures stack, allocations or iteration counts has this shape and none of the others has been checked. — evidence: _scratchpad/pass2_r5_213211/</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-20 — CONFIRMED — THE AUDIT THIS ROW ASKED FOR IS DONE, AND ITS ANSWER IS &#x27;memory_rw IS THE ONLY ONE&#x27;. Four other differentials mention &#x27;stack&#x27; and EVERY mention is PROSE -- descriptions of the SUBJECT&#x27;s stack use (diff_diskimage_io.c:306), or of an argument that must not be a stack array (:350, diff_diskimage_sync.c:312), or a reference to #410&#x27;s stack-leak reasoning (diff_wdc_identify.c:123,154), or the phrase &#x27;defence-in-depth&#x27; (diff_diskimage_geom.c:73). None measures a resource. Comments were stripped before matching, so prose cannot masquerade as a measurement.
tools/pipeline\matrix.html:956:Harm if reached: emulated clock frozen -- hz=0 -&gt; timer_clamp_freq floors to TIMER_MIN_FREQUENCY = 1e-8 Hz, one tick per 3.17 years. — evidence: git show 1ce189c --stat; dev_8253.c I8253_TIMER_MSB arm</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-held"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-held"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">m8probe</span><span class="ttl">m8probe  m8820x PROBE_USER/PROBE_SUPER are dropped, so SSR answers a deterministic miss</span><span class="tip">m8probe  m8820x PROBE_USER/PROBE_SUPER are dropped, so SSR answers a deterministic miss — HOLD: *** RE-FILED LATENT 2026-08-26 ON THE `gdrompiooddlen` PRECEDENT -- REACHABILITY MEASURED NEGATIVE, WITH CONTROLS IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. MUST NOT BE RANKED LIVE. *** A full OpenBSD 7.7/luna88k boot to `login:` (7,684,964,995 instructions) issues **seven distinct CMMU commands and ZERO probes**. Denominator stated: 0 of 7 distinct commands, not 0 of 0 -- and it independently replicates #433&#x27;s finding thirty rounds later. **The controls are what make this evidence:** a real guest supervisor store on a cold debugger, with the planted word DISASSEMBLED BEFORE STEPPING per the hand-assembled-encoding rule -- cmd 0x24 and 0x20 fire the detector, cmd 0x35 does not while still registering as M8CMD_FIRST. So the negative is real and not a broken grep. CORROBORATION that sharpens it past &#x27;this guest does not&#x27;: OpenBSD&#x27;s m88k CMMU driver issues CMMU_PROBE from exactly two places and **both are inside DDB display routines** -- a kernel-debugger feature, not an operating path, reachable only by a human at a DDB prompt. (Caveat recorded by the seat: that source is OpenBSD 2.2/mvme88k, the lineage, not the booting guest; the boot measurement is the evidence for the actual guest.) *** THE OLD COST NOTE WAS WRONG AND IS CORRECTED HERE. *** &#x27;Needs the translation walk&#x27; implies a CAPABILITY gap. **The walk exists** -- m88k_translate_v2p() at memory_m88k.c:103 -- **and is already side-effect-free under FLAG_NOEXCEPTIONS** (:344 guards the PG_U/PG_M writeback, :374 returns before any PFSR/PFAR write), its flags already cover the probe&#x27;s own selectors, and the SSR bit layout is in-tree. **And the driving probe SHAPE is already committed**: m8820x_sites_probe.py:159 ships a PROBE_SUPER row driven by one real guest instruction, ~3 s, no boot. *This is the `sh4dmacie` situation in reverse -- there the shape was missing and it was mis-read as a capability gap; here the shape was already there and nobody re-read the probe.* **WHAT IS ACTUALLY MISSING IS AN ORACLE, AND THE HOLD IS NOW CONDITIONAL ON IT:** translate_v2p exposes no BATC-vs-PATC-vs-walk distinction (needed for CMMU_SSR_BH) and none of the U/M/PROT/SO attributes SSR must carry; real probe semantics are supported only by DDB code reading those registers, which is evidence and not proof; and **there is no 88200/88204 manual in this project**. TRIGGER, on the SH4_VAL_NCLASS precedent: **if an 88200/88204 manual is obtained, this becomes a small round.** That converts an indefinite hold into a conditional one. *** AND THE CURRENT BEHAVIOUR IS THE BETTER ONE, which is the strongest reason not to rank it: *** a dropped probe leaves SSR zero with the V bit clear -- a deterministic, DEFINED &#x27;no valid translation&#x27;. Implementing without the manual would replace a defined conservative miss with an INVENTED answer that could steer the guest&#x27;s paging. **That is the same reasoning used to decline `sh4aaalias` before the SH manual arrived -- and that one turned out to be a wrong finding.** The only known consumer prints a line in a debugger display, so a cosmetically wrong DDB line for a human is the entire measured consequence. WORTH ADDING CHEAPLY: one row asserting SSR == 0 after a probe, to pin the DELIBERATE behaviour that today rests on prose in two comments and no oracle at all. — witness: none -- LATENT. The claim is true by reading, but the path is unreached by any operating guest OS, so no rung-3/4 witness can be built without first constructing a guest that probes. — note: *** EVIDENCE 2026-08-27: the claim is TRUE and the path is COMPLETELY UNREACHED by operating guest OS paths. Latent. ***
tools/pipeline\matrix.html:3616:**A BOUNDED STRENGTHENING IS AVAILABLE, and it is verified against the real instance:** for each added `file.ext:NNN`, if THAT FILE IS ALSO MODIFIED BY THE SAME DIFF, warn -- the commit&#x27;s own hunks move the lines, so the citation is at risk BY CONSTRUCTION. **MEASURED: `git show --name-only 5b5089d` lists `src/devices/dev_dreamcast_gdrom.c`, so the rule fires on today&#x27;s case.** It must be a WARN and not a FAIL: correctness is undecidable, and a self-citation into an edited file is sometimes right. Cost is a few lines beside the existing D loop.
