**VERDICT: The core claim is true. The gate mixes staged filenames with working-tree contents. Section D is worse: it ignores staged additions even when everything is staged.**

Your proposed subset commit establishes that the snapshots differ. It does **not**, by itself, establish that the difference changes a check’s verdict. However, the permitted harness source records an actual shipped inconsistency of this class.

**Q1. The input selection is mixed.** [The changed-file selection](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/precommit_check.sh:881) says:

```bash
CHANGED=$(git diff --cached --name-only)
if [ -z "$CHANGED" ]; then
	CHANGED=$(git status --porcelain -z | tr '\0' '\n' | sed -e 's/^...//' -e 's/.* -> //')
fi
```

That selects **names**, principally for A/B/C/E and the hook controls. It does not select which version of those files subsequent commands read.

Representative actual reads are:

```bash
elif cmp -s "$SEC/$f" "$EST/$f"; then
```

That is [A reading filesystem bytes](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/precommit_check.sh:981).

```bash
ADDED=$(git diff -U0 | grep '^+' | grep -v '^+++')
```

That is [D collecting unstaged additions](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/precommit_check.sh:1157).

```python
ledger = json.load(io.open(LEDGER, encoding="utf-8"))
text = io.open(BUGS, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace").read()
```

Those are [P’s filesystem reads](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/check_bugfile_sync.py:103).

There is **no indexed-blob reader such as `git show :<path>` in the invoked checking paths**. There are genuine index-membership checks through `git ls-files`, and historical queries through `git log`. L’s `git show` retrieves filenames from an existing commit, not staged file contents.

Some comments explain filename selection. They do not establish one consistent snapshot for the gate.

**Q2. Almost every content check is affected, with important exceptions.** In this table, **FG/FR** means working-tree corrections can conceal an invalid indexed version, while reversing that divergence can reject a valid indexed version. These are possibilities under each check’s existing predicate, not findings that today’s files violate it.

| Section | Actual inputs | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| [A](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/precommit_check.sh:967) — propagation | Staged-selected source names; filesystem allowlist and SEC/est bytes | **FG/FR.** Propagated working-tree bytes do not establish that staged source matches est. |
| [B](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/precommit_check.sh:1002) — build trees | Filesystem SEC/build/build-asan/WSL source comparisons; external sentinels | **FG/FR** for source correspondence. Sentinel presence is independently a local operational check. |
| [C](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/precommit_check.sh:1137) — message paths | Message file plus `CHANGED` names | **Correctly uses staged membership when anything is staged.** It makes no content-level guarantee. Before staging, it checks preview names. |
| [D1/D2](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/precommit_check.sh:1157) — citations/counts | Unstaged added lines; indexed filename lookup; filesystem `wc -l` | **FG/FR. Fully staging everything empties the added-line input.** |
| [E](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/precommit_check.sh:1201) — detector identity | Selected detector names; `grep` of working files | **FG/FR** for the identity marker. E2 is only a reminder. |
| [F](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/precommit_check.sh:841) — receipt | Historical source-commit SHA; filesystem `pass2_ledger.tsv` | **FG/FR.** An unstaged receipt can satisfy the check. Its historical target is intentional. |
| [G](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/check_seats_read.py:103) — recorded answers | Working ledger; external panel-file existence and sizes | **FG/FR** through unstaged ledger corrections. |
| [H](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/check_stage_panels.py:104) — stage completeness | Working ledger | **FG/FR** for recorded completeness and holds. |
| [I](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/check_fable_queue.py:54) — owed work queued | Working ledger and queue | **FG/FR** for their relationship. |
| [I2](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/gen_codex_wall.py:184) — generated queue summary | Working ledger, generator and queue | **FG/FR.** Agreement on disk does not establish agreement in the index. |
